{
  "description": "The proving lab of the resilient mesh (C-operations 2.9 and 7: rolls of every tier, crashes, the contributors' changes, replace, the autoscaler on Linode, scored by the referee's change-window.py), merged topology: in each region two forwarders and 4 edges in sydney, 4 edges in london, 4 edges in newyork, 4 edges in tokyo, all g6-dedicated-2; listener load hosts 1 x g6-dedicated-8 in sydney, 1 x g6-dedicated-8 in london, 1 x g6-dedicated-8 in newyork, 1 x g6-dedicated-8 in tokyo (needletail-load for the UDP listeners, ntcmp for the LL-HLS ones) and a g6-dedicated-4 view host for the full probes, on the region's VLAN (Linode does not bill VLAN traffic; 5,000 UDP listeners of 1 ms PCM over the public network would be about 12 TB an hour of billed transfer), and a self-hosted LiveKit SFU (g6-dedicated-2) per region; the contributor alone on a g6-dedicated-4 in London, its standby contrib-lon-b alone on another (both publish the same parts) with its source host lon-src. Dedicated plans only. Sydney first: the core of the region short of capacity is created first; the run works without it (lab up --optional-sites sydney, or --without-sites sydney). The listener hosts are created last, in batches: the lab is kept when the account refuses some (listeners_missing), and scale-run.py fits its steps to the hosts that exist. Standby edges (syd-edge-4, lon-edge-4, new-edge-4, tok-edge-4): created, held out by the deploy setting standby_edges until they are started in (deploy start --nodes, or the autoscaler). Autoscale slots (syd-dist-c, syd-edge-5, lon-dist-c, lon-edge-5, new-dist-c, new-edge-5, tok-dist-c, tok-edge-5): in every peer list from the first push, created only by the autoscaler (lab add), never by up or grow. Three serving edges and one standby edge a region for the kill and roll rows (agreed with the referee, 23 November). Generated by scripts/scale_topology.py; run as C-operations section 7 says, under the lab tool's watchdog and budget.",
